WEBVTT

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.450
Hey, are you ready yet?

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.620
Sorry, I still don't know what to wear.

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.330
Come on!
Normally, it's girls who make boys wait.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.200
I want new clothes.

00:00:32.450 --> 00:00:36.410
Did you know the latest update
comes with new outfits?

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:39.080
I'm sure you'll like them.

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:44.290
You'll purchase them for me, right?

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.200
PROCEED TO PURCHASE PAID CONTENTS?

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:48.000
Aw, Seiya,

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:50.500
you're so good at convincing me!

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:53.950
-How's this?
-Yes, please!

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.370
-And this?
-Get it!

00:00:55.450 --> 00:00:57.410
-Should I extend my horn?
 -Definitely!

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.370
It'll be 10% cheaper if you buy 20.

00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:03.750
I'll buy them all!

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:07.290
TOTAL SAVINGS

00:01:08.290 --> 00:01:09.200
RAGE

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:05.120
<i>Just count to ten</i>

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.370
<i>and I'll be a model employee.</i>

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.120
Good morning!

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:19.120
Good morning, Retsuko!

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:20.950
Morning, Retsuko.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.540
Oh, good. I made it in time...

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:26.000
What's with your face?

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.330
Is it that bad?

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:28.250
Yeah.

00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:30.250
My alarm didn't go off this morning.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.660
There was no time for makeup
or even a look in the mirror.

00:02:32.750 --> 00:02:34.250
That's not what I meant.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.450
I'm gonna do my makeup in the bathroom.

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.830
I'll be going!

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:47.540
That was close.

00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:49.620
I hope she didn't notice.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:53.540
Retsuko's been rather cheerful lately.

00:02:53.620 --> 00:02:56.580
Maybe she has a new boyfriend already!

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:58.790
I'm not sure...

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:00.370
ACCOUNTING DEPARTMENT

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:03.200
Hmm? Your makeup is quite thick today.

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:05.870
Is that so?
Maybe you're imagining things.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:10.200
So about that social mixer next month...
Are you going?

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.370
The admission is 5,000 yen, isn't it?

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.290
Yup.

00:03:13.370 --> 00:03:14.410
Hmm...

00:03:14.830 --> 00:03:18.160
I'll pass.
I've spent too much money this month.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.870
What? You're not going, Retsuko?

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:23.450
Why not?
Did you go on a big shopping spree?

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:26.500
Well, you know, it was just... stuff.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:28.200
Like clothes?

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:31.250
Yeah, something like that.

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:33.410
What about you, Haida?

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:36.580
I think I'll pass, too.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:37.870
I thought so.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:42.870
Did that mark go away?

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:45.250
Yeah, somewhat.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:47.750
Correct me if I'm wrong,

00:03:48.200 --> 00:03:49.750
but here's my theory...

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:57.910
After your romance with Mr. Tadano ended,

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.870
it left a big hole in your heart.

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:05.250
<i>To fill that void,</i>
<i>you found a virtual boyfriend.</i>

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:08.950
<i>You became a loyal spender and dozed off</i>
<i>with your goggles on last night,</i>

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:11.160
<i>which brings us to today.</i>

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.750
Well?

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:16.000
Huh? How did you come up
with such a ridiculous story?

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.580
Don't be silly!

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.040
20,000 yen?

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.750
Just yesterday?
For clothes you can't wear?

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.450
It was actually 18,000 yen
after the 10% discount.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:27.620
That changes nothing!

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.330
You're on track to screw yourself over
with such reckless spending.

00:04:31.830 --> 00:04:35.080
Don't worry.
I'm doing it within my means.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.450
You're being a sucker.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:37.950
I know that.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.040
No, you don't!

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:45.160
I won't take any more risks.

00:04:45.830 --> 00:04:46.660
Huh?

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.040
I don't have any special talents,

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.250
so I'll live with my feet on the ground.

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:56.040
I'll just accept my place in life
and not aim for more.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:59.580
I'm just going to work
so I can live a mediocre life.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:01.830
Okay...

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:05.080
But...

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:09.040
even you couldn't stand
such a dull life, could you?

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:12.500
That's why I pay money
for one dream-like moment!

00:05:12.580 --> 00:05:16.200
It gives me strength for the next day!
Is that bad?

00:05:16.290 --> 00:05:20.250
And spending money on a bum
like your virtual boyfriend isn't dull?

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:22.660
Don't you dare talk bad about Seiya!

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.040
Oh, you're in deep.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:31.450
It's nobody's business
how I spend the money that I earn.

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:33.830
Right, Seiya?

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:42.750
<i>You're on track to screw yourself over</i>
<i>with such reckless spending.</i>

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:47.830
In short,
it all comes down to will power!

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:51.080
If I decide not to do it,
then that's the end of the story.

00:05:51.830 --> 00:05:53.410
I won't buy anything today!

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.000
It's settled!

00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:00.750
Oh, Seiya, I'm home!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.200
Aw, you're wearing the clothes I got you.

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:07.660
I'm not buying anything for you today.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:09.540
Not today!

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.660
I'm not buying anything!

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:20.580
What is Retsuko doing?

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:22.330
She's eating bread crusts.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:25.910
I thought so!
The ones that bakeries give away, right?

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.910
Hey, Retsuko.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.330
What's wrong? Are you alive?

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:35.000
200,000 yen.

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:36.500
200,000 yen?

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.660
What? You wasted 200,000 yen
on in-game items to win a luxury prize?

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:45.580
You didn't win,

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:48.700
but you were listed as a top-paying user,
and Seiya praised you?

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:50.040
Are you stupid?

00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:51.620
TOTAL SAVINGS

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:53.950
WOMEN'S CHANGING ROOM

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.160
I was stupid.

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:56.540
Yeah.

00:06:58.040 --> 00:07:00.450
But I might buy one of Seiya's albums.

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:03.700
What's super rare is that
you get a real CD, not just a download!

00:07:03.790 --> 00:07:04.700
Isn't that amazing?

00:07:04.790 --> 00:07:06.250
Do you have a CD player?

00:07:06.330 --> 00:07:07.500
No...

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:13.410
If you're forced to eat bread crusts,
why don't you borrow from Anai?

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:14.660
What?

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:17.620
Apparently, he's going to publish a book.

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:19.250
A book? Why?

00:07:19.660 --> 00:07:21.000
He's good at cooking, right?

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.660
He posted
his lunch recipes online every day

00:07:23.750 --> 00:07:26.000
and was contacted by a publisher.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:28.290
Wow, that's amazing.

00:07:28.700 --> 00:07:30.370
A side hustle, you know?

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:33.700
Making the most of your talents
outside of your main job.

00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:37.330
He's making a little extra money,
so maybe he can help you out.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:42.330
I have enough to pay the rent,
so I'll survive.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:44.160
If you say so.

00:07:44.910 --> 00:07:47.410
I haven't fallen so low
that I'd need help from a junior.

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:49.370
Oh, you've fallen low enough.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:07:59.450
<i>A side hustle, huh? That's great.</i>

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.250
<i>I don't have the skills</i>
<i>or energy for that.</i>

00:08:05.870 --> 00:08:07.910
Retsuko, do you want to invest?

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:09.700
Invest?

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:12.580
What's this, all of a sudden?

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.290
She's been
super into her side hustle lately.

00:08:16.370 --> 00:08:19.660
She's starting a company with
a programmer friend to develop an app.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.410
You have a side hustle, too?

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.830
And developing an app
is such a serious business!

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:27.830
I know.

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:30.540
It's still in the trial stage but...
Ta-da!

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:31.750
GORI'S MARRIAGE COUNSELING

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:32.830
<i>What's this?</i>

00:08:32.910 --> 00:08:34.500
<i>It's a matchmaking app.</i>

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:40.000
I've lost hope
in this country's matchmaking scene.

00:08:40.410 --> 00:08:44.200
Age, income... What's the point
in matching up numbers like that?

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:48.790
What's important is a fateful encounter
with your soul mate!

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:51.750
This is my revenge
on the matchmaking industry.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:56.000
With years of experience as my weapon,
I'll change this country!

00:08:56.080 --> 00:08:58.330
And I'll use
this innovative app to do it!

00:09:00.700 --> 00:09:02.000
So how is it innovative?

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.660
Well, that's next on our list.

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:07.580
You look like you're enjoying yourself.

00:09:07.660 --> 00:09:11.750
It's really fun!
I get to discover my own potential!

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:13.950
Don't let it affect your day job, okay?

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:15.700
I know!

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:18.750
So, do you want to invest?

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:21.200
Well, um...

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:22.950
I'm sorry.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:24.330
I...

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:26.450
don't have any money.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.750
What in the world is Retsuko eating?

00:09:36.830 --> 00:09:39.250
Probably something worse
than bread crusts.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:40.620
BREAK ROOM

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:43.290
What? A virtual boyfriend?

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.080
Yeah. Funny, right?

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:50.250
You shouldn't flaunt people's
embarrassing secrets like that.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:52.410
I thought I should tell you.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.620
This could be your shot.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:58.330
A chance to sneak into that hole
in Retsuko's heart.

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:03.040
I don't really like to take advantage
of people like that.

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:05.580
Are you trying to make yourself look good?

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.750
So you're still gonna wait, huh?

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:11.000
Do you think she'll come to you
because you're acting nice?

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:16.410
-I... want to play it fair, like a man!
-Play it fair by doing what?

00:10:16.500 --> 00:10:18.620
By asking her out for drinks as a friend,

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.540
just to get rejected again?

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.580
You're being naive.

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:26.160
Someone's going
to be single again this year!

00:10:30.950 --> 00:10:33.160
ACCOUNTING DEPARTMENT

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:42.000
What are you doing?

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:42.950
Typing up a draft.

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:44.200
A draft?

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.620
It's a column for my upcoming book.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:51.370
It's okay to be passionate
about your side job,

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.700
but don't neglect your real job.

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:55.660
I've finished all my tasks.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.000
I see.

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:03.830
You seem kind of... different.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.620
What do you mean?

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.500
Do you...

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:10.830
have a girlfriend or something?

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.120
Yes,

00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:13.410
I do.

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:16.870
Oh... I see.

00:11:20.160 --> 00:11:22.540
I haven't been eating properly
the last few days.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:29.790
MOM

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:31.870
Hello.

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:35.790
<i>Retsuko? How are you doing?</i>
<i>Are you eating well?</i>

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:37.540
I'm at work right now!

00:11:38.000 --> 00:11:39.000
<i>I see.</i>

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:42.040
<i>Anyway, I know this is short notice,</i>

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:44.330
<i>but can you drive me to the hot spring?</i>

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:45.950
The hot spring?

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:47.750
OX RENTAL CARS

00:11:47.830 --> 00:11:50.120
<i>I was counting on your father to drive,</i>

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.580
<i>but he has to attend a funeral</i>
<i>all of a sudden!</i>

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:57.250
<i>I've already booked a place,</i>
<i>so why don't you come instead?</i>

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:59.910
<i>Is that okay?</i>
<i>I'll pay you for your time, of course.</i>

00:12:00.370 --> 00:12:02.290
I'll gladly do it!

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.830
White rice! So tasty!

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:19.500
What do you normally eat?

00:12:24.790 --> 00:12:26.950
<i>The blessings... of life.</i>

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:33.700
You don't want to come in?

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:37.000
No, I want to return the car
before it gets dark.

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.290
You're so boring.

00:12:38.370 --> 00:12:39.870
Well, I can't help that.

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.450
Well, then, take this.
It's not much, but...

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.500
<i>Whoa, there's 20,000 yen here.</i>

00:12:58.410 --> 00:13:02.620
<i>Thank goodness.</i>
<i>Now I can survive the month.</i>

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:09.870
KEEP IT TOGETHER! - MOM

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:17.290
All right, I just have to return this car
to the rental office, and then I'm done!

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:25.410
Another of life's blessings.

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.160
What was that?

00:13:36.750 --> 00:13:40.660
Oh, it's just a wheel stop.
Phew! I was really worried there.

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:43.410
Let's try going forward.

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:55.870
<i>Why?</i>

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:58.120
<i>Why?</i>

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:03.200
<i>A painful mistake...</i>

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:24.750
Um, I'm sorry. Are you all right?

00:14:25.750 --> 00:14:27.450
Quit mumbling...

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:28.790
and get out the car.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:00.620
Subtitle translation by: Rachael Momber
